Source: https://github.com/ouch-org/ouch
Comment: The binary ouch is compiled from the release named in the control
 file, unchanged, with its default features. It links in the Rust crates
 listed in its Cargo.lock, each under its own license. The license file of
 ouch is in /usr/share/doc/ouch/LICENSE.
 .
 The default feature unrar links in the UnRAR source code of Alexander
 Roshal, through the crate unrar-ng-sys, for decompressing and listing RAR
 archives. Its license allows that, but forbids using the code to recreate
 the RAR compression algorithm, so the package is not free software under
 the Debian Free Software Guidelines.

